From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: rearm GPON receiver once after LOS

The LOS-specific TO2 path fully disables both the MAC and the digital PHY,
then expects an SFP link-up notification to restart them.  Integrated GPON
front ends cannot produce that notification after the PHY has been powered
off, so reconnecting the fibre leaves the ONU permanently in O1.

Schedule one restart after the orderly shutdown.  The restarted PHY remains
in O2 while LOS is asserted and its existing link poll can then observe the
fibre returning.  This is a single rearm, not a periodic restart loop.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -5070,6 +5070,10 @@ static void gpon_to2_work_fn(struct work_
 		dev_warn(priv->dev,
 			 "GPON TO2 expired in O6 with the optical link still down, waiting for the fibre\n");
 		gpon_disable(priv);
+		if (READ_ONCE(priv->started) &&
+		    READ_ONCE(priv->optical_active))
+			mod_delayed_work(priv->fsm_wq, &priv->restart_work,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(GPON_DEACTIVATE_RESTART_MS));
 		return;
 	}
 
